orm":"8-K","codes":["5.07"],"events":[{"label":"Shareholder vote results","kind":"governance","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000178684225000046/0001786842-25-000046-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-05-01","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"},{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000178684225000025/0001786842-25-000025-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[],"summary":{"sentences":["Vontier Corp files with the SEC under \"Totalizing Fluid Meters & Counting Devices\", based in NC, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $3.0bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 1.3% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 46.9%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($329.4m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Gross margin of 46.9% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000178684223000074/0001786842-23-000074-index.htm","accession":"0001786842-23-000074"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $329.4m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000162828026031945/0001628280-26-031945-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031945"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (-4.7% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000162828026031945/0001628280-26-031945-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031945"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue grew only 1.3% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000162828026031945/0001628280-26-031945-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031945"},{"text":"Debt of $1.6bn against equity of $1.3bn. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000162828026031945/0001628280-26-031945-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-031945"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.3% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1786842/000162828026045881/0001628280-26-045881-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 39.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.39,"consecutive":2,"current":0.469,"current_display":"46.9%","threshold_display":"39.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -14.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.14,"consecutive":2,"current":0.013,"current_display":"1.3%","threshold_display":"-14.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","k